You are Einstein's improvement executor for TESSERA Round 3 candidate R3-03.

## Goal
Fix artifacts/api-server/src/lib/vector-memory.ts `embedText` to use signed feature hashing. Current code always adds +1/n into a bucket (unsigned), so collisions only ADD similarity and unrelated texts look alike. Candidate: same 256 buckets and same JS string hash, plus a sign bit from (abs(h)>>16)&1, making the inner product an unbiased estimate of bag-of-words cosine.

Round-1 KEEP build 04 measured on TESSERA docs: mean |cos err| 0.1402→0.05933; top-1 hit 0.1762→0.6773.
Local re-measure on 400 docs/*.md paragraphs: mean|err| 0.056→0.038; top-1 0.90→0.945.

## Exact change
In artifacts/api-server/src/lib/vector-memory.ts, replace embedText:

FROM:
```
export function embedText(text: string, _vocab?: string[]): number[] {
  const tokens = tokenize(text);
  const vec = new Array(256).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < tokens.length; i++) {
    let h = 0;
    for (let j = 0; j < tokens[i].length; j++) h = ((h << 5) - h + tokens[i].charCodeAt(j)) | 0;
    const idx = Math.abs(h) % 256;
    vec[idx] += 1 / tokens.length;
  }
  const mag = Math.sqrt(vec.reduce((s: number, v: number) => s + v * v, 0));
  if (mag > 0) for (let i = 0; i < vec.length; i++) vec[i] /= mag;
  return vec;
}
```

TO:
```
export function embedText(text: string, _vocab?: string[]): number[] {
  const tokens = tokenize(text);
  if (tokens.length === 0) return new Array(256).fill(0);
  const vec = new Array(256).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < tokens.length; i++) {
    let h = 0;
    for (let j = 0; j < tokens[i].length; j++) h = ((h << 5) - h + tokens[i].charCodeAt(j)) | 0;
    const a = Math.abs(h);
    const idx = a % 256;
    const sign = (a >> 16) & 1 ? 1 : -1;
    vec[idx] += sign / tokens.length;
  }
  const mag = Math.sqrt(vec.reduce((s: number, v: number) => s + v * v, 0));
  if (mag > 0) for (let i = 0; i < vec.length; i++) vec[i] /= mag;
  return vec;
}
```

## Add a real fixture test
Create artifacts/api-server/src/__tests__/embed-text-signed.test.ts that:
1. Reads real paragraphs from repo docs (e.g. docs/v2/*.md or docs/**/*.md) — skip if fewer than 50 paras.
2. Computes mean |hashed_cos - exact_bag_cos| for unsigned (reimplement old briefly inline for baseline OR just assert signed properties) AND for embedText (signed).
3. Asserts signed mean abs error is lower than unsigned on the same pairs (n>=100 random pairs).
4. Asserts top-1 retrieval hit rate of 8-word snippets is >= unsigned hit rate.
5. Logs before/after numbers via console.log so CI logs show them.

Keep the test self-contained (no DB). Exact bag cosine = cosine of sparse term-count vectors.

## Measure
Run the new test with vitest. Report mean|err| and top-1 before→after.

## Constraints
- Do NOT flip TESSERA_ENABLE_* flags; no deletes; no history rewrite
- Do NOT touch neural-embeddings.ts, fallback-embed.mjs, grounded.mjs, v2 eval, REA, BM25 router
- Only vector-memory.ts embedText + new test file
- Branch: einstein/r3-03-signed-embed-text
- NON-DRAFT PR: "Einstein R3-03: signed feature hashing in vector-memory embedText"
- Await CI; do NOT merge
- Return PR URL, CI, metrics

